{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>With abominations they provoked Him to anger.</b> They kindled His wrath with abominations and repugnant deeds such as male homosexual intercourse and sorcery, which contain an abomination — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 32:16). And so it is found in the Sifrei (Ha'azinu, paragraph 335). But there is no reproof in this song except concerning idolatry alone. And the reason for <b>בְּזָרִים</b> (foreigners): it is drawn after <b>אֱלוֹהַּ עָשָׂהוּ</b> (a foreign god provoked Him to jealousy) — they provoked Him with foreign gods, in the sense of <b>אֱלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים</b> (other gods). And the reason for <b>בְּתוֹעֵבוֹת</b> (abominations): the demons — to burn their children in the fire for other gods, for all this is abominable before Him, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 12:31), 'For every abomination of YHWH that He hates they did for their gods, for even their sons and their daughters they burn in the fire for their gods,' and it is written (Jeremiah 32:35), 'which I did not command them, nor did it enter My heart, to do this abominable deed.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:44.556592851Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}